  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1238 PM CDT Wed Oct 14 2026\n\nA break in activity to the west is expected as the morning \nconvection moves east into eastern Oklahoma and northwest \nArkansas with a gradual lessening in intensity and rainfall\namounts with time. Enough of a lull may exist for instability to \nreturn across the area as the main cold front moves through late \nafternoon into the evening Thursday. Additional scattered showers \nand storms are expected to accompany the front though wind fields \nwill be sub-par and updrafts will be undercut reducing the severe \nthreat. Small hail or occasional wind gusts will be the main\nthreat with stronger updrafts.\n\nDry and much cooler air will move in behind the front starting\nThursday night with our first real taste of fall weather as lows\ndrop into the 40s and lower 50s. Strong northerly winds will be on\ntap for Friday with widespread gusts of 30 to 35 mph forecast.\nLater shifts may need to consider a wind advisory or yet, fire\nweather headlines across far southeast Oklahoma if earlier\nrainfall does not pan out. Afternoon highs both Friday and\nSaturday will be in the 50s and 60s before southerly winds return\nand a gradual warming trend begins into early next week.",
